# Force LF line endings for all text files on every platform.
#
# Goldens and fixtures are byte-compared, and some (the CK wire vector at
# crates/broca-ck/tests/fixtures/ck_wire_golden.json) are cross-language parser inputs, so
# their on-disk bytes MUST be identical regardless of the checkout OS. Without this, a
# Windows checkout rewrites LF to CRLF and a multi-line golden fails byte-exact comparison
# (serde_json always emits LF) — which broke the Windows CI leg. The repo is authored
# LF-only, so this introduces no renormalization on Unix.
* text=auto eol=lf
crates/broca-provider/tests/fixtures/codex_resume_turn_with_echoed_reasoning.json -text
crates/broca-provider/tests/fixtures/codex_reasoning_turn_response.sse -text
crates/broca-provider/tests/fixtures/codex_toolcall_turn_function_call_pairing.json -text
crates/broca-provider/tests/fixtures/cc_system_reminder_request.json -text
crates/broca-provider/tests/fixtures/codex_spark_toolcall_done_only.sse -text
# Sealed WAL archive containers are binary fixtures pinned by digest.
*.ark binary
